---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import imgSettings from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-01-settings-system.jpg';
import imgPicker from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-02-firmware-picker.jpg';
import imgConfirm from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-03-confirm.jpg';
import imgUpdating from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-04-updating.jpg';
import imgComplete from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-05-complete.jpg';
import imgHome from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-06-home.jpg';
import imgApps from '../../../assets/photos/goto-install-07-apps.jpg';

const releaseUrl = 'https://github.com/archievalmariano/crosspoint-reader/releases/tag/v1.0.2';
const downloadUrl = 'https://github.com/archievalmariano/crosspoint-reader/releases/download/v1.0.2/firmware-x4-g.bin';
const sourceUrl = 'https://github.com/archievalmariano/crosspoint-reader/tree/v1.0.2';
const fileName = 'firmware-x4-g.bin';
const sha256 = '63f82f49da7ea7d1e8a19a1b96ef1daccf589ce995b313c7c215c796e12aaa77';
const stepWidths = [400, 620, 820];
const stepSizes = '(max-width: 520px) 88vw, 400px';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Install Project GOTO on the XTEINK X4 — Archieval Mariano"
  description="An illustrated guide to installing Project GOTO (release v1.0.2) on the XTEINK X4 using CrossPoint Reader's SD card firmware updater."
>
  <section class="wrap install">
    <p class="install__back"><a href="/goto/">&larr; Project GOTO</a></p>

    <header class="install__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Project GOTO</p>
      <h1>Install Project GOTO on the XTEINK X4</h1>
    </header>

    <p class="install__lede">
      Project GOTO is built for the XTEINK X4 running CrossPoint Reader 1.6.0. The
      current release is v1.0.2 (CrossPoint 1.6.0 + Apps 1.0.2), with GOTO in the
      Apps menu.
    </p>
    <p class="install__lede">
      Installation uses CrossPoint Reader’s built-in SD card firmware updater. You do
      not need to run a server, clone a repository, or configure the hosted service.
    </p>

    <dl class="install__meta">
      <div><dt>Firmware</dt><dd><code>{fileName}</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt>SHA-256</dt><dd><code class="install__sha">{sha256}</code></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="install__actions">
      <a class="install__download" href={downloadUrl}>Download {fileName}</a>
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul class="install__list">
        <li>an XTEINK X4</li>
        <li>CrossPoint Reader already installed</li>
        <li>a microSD card readable by the X4</li>
        <li><code>{fileName}</code></li>
        <li>Wi-Fi for retrieving the current edition</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="install__note">This file is for the original XTEINK X4. The X4 Pro installs over USB instead: see the <a href="/goto/install/x4-pro/">X4 Pro guide</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>1. Copy the firmware to the microSD card</h2>
      <p>
        Download <code>{fileName}</code> and place it in the root of the
        microSD card, not inside a folder.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you already keep an official CrossPoint X4 firmware image on the card, you
        may leave it there as the intended rollback option.
      </p>
      <p class="install__caption-lead">macOS:</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>{'COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 cp firmware-x4-g.bin "/Volumes/<YOUR_SD>/"'}</code></pre>
      <p>
        If a <code>{'._firmware-x4-g.bin'}</code> file appears, remove it before
        ejecting the card.
      </p>
      <p>Safely eject the microSD card, then insert it into the X4.</p>

      <h3 class="install__subhead">Optional: verify the download</h3>
      <p>The file’s SHA-256 checksum should be:</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>{sha256}</code></pre>
      <p class="install__caption-lead">macOS:</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>shasum -a 256 firmware-x4-g.bin</code></pre>
      <p class="install__caption-lead">Linux:</p>
      <pre class="install__code"><code>sha256sum firmware-x4-g.bin</code></pre>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>2. Open the firmware updater</h2>
      <p>On the X4, open Settings &rarr; System &rarr; SD Card Firmware Update.</p>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgSettings} alt="The XTEINK X4 Settings screen on the System tab, with SD Card Firmware Update highlighted and the version 1.6.0-A1.0.2-G in the header." widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Open Settings, switch to System, then select SD Card Firmware Update.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>3. Select the Project GOTO firmware</h2>
      <p>In the firmware picker, select <code>{fileName}</code>.</p>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgPicker} alt="The firmware file picker on the XTEINK X4 with firmware-x4-g.bin selected, below CROSSPOINT_OFFICIAL_X4.bin." widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Select firmware-x4-g.bin from the microSD card.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>4. Confirm the update</h2>
      <p>
        The X4 will validate the firmware and show a confirmation screen. Check that
        the filename is <code>{fileName}</code>, then select Confirm.
      </p>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgConfirm} alt="The XTEINK X4 confirmation dialog reading Update firmware? for firmware-x4-g.bin, with Confirm selected." widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Confirm the update after checking the firmware filename.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>5. Wait for installation to finish</h2>
      <p>The X4 will begin installing the firmware.</p>
      <p class="install__warn">Do not power off the device while the update is in progress.</p>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgUpdating} alt="The XTEINK X4 SD Card Firmware Update screen showing Updating… 0% and Do not power off!" widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Leave the X4 powered on while the firmware is being installed.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>6. Let the X4 restart</h2>
      <p>When installation finishes, the X4 will display Update complete and restart.</p>
      <p>
        If it does not restart automatically, follow the on-screen instruction and
        hold the power button for a few seconds.
      </p>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgComplete} alt="The XTEINK X4 showing Update complete and a restarting message." widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Once the update completes, allow the X4 to restart.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>7. Open Project GOTO</h2>
      <p>
        After reboot, the CrossPoint home screen has an <strong>Apps</strong> entry.
        Open Apps, then select <strong>GOTO</strong>. In the evening it reads
        <strong>TOGO</strong>, after the evening edition.
      </p>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgHome} alt="The CrossPoint Reader home screen on the XTEINK X4 with Apps highlighted below Settings." widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Apps appears on the CrossPoint home screen after installation.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="install__figure">
        <Image src={imgApps} alt="The Apps screen on the XTEINK X4 listing TOGO, the evening edition of GOTO." widths={stepWidths} sizes={stepSizes} format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Inside Apps, GOTO reads TOGO once the evening edition is out.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>You can also confirm the installed version in the Settings header:</p>
      <p class="install__version"><code>1.6.0-A1.0.2-G</code></p>
      <figure class="install__figure install__figure--small">
        <Image src={imgSettings} alt="The XTEINK X4 Settings header showing the version string 1.6.0-A1.0.2-G." widths={[260, 420, 520]} sizes="(max-width: 520px) 60vw, 260px" format="webp" quality={74} loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>The installed version shown in Settings.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="install__note">
        <code>1.6.0</code> is the CrossPoint base, <code>A1.0.2</code> the release, and
        <code>G</code> the package (GOTO).
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>First launch</h2>
      <p>Connect the X4 to Wi-Fi, then open Apps → GOTO.</p>
      <p>
        Project GOTO will retrieve the current edition from the hosted service and
        save a local cached copy after a successful fetch.
      </p>
      <p>
        A saved Wi-Fi network may occasionally need to be reconnected manually after
        sleep or reboot on the X4/CrossPoint environment. If GOTO cannot reach the
        service, reconnect through CrossPoint’s Wi-Fi settings and reopen GOTO.
      </p>
      <p>Previously cached editions remain readable without a new fetch.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>Using Project GOTO</h2>
      <p>GOTO is the morning edition, normally published around 06:00 PHT.</p>
      <p>TOGO is the evening edition, normally published around 18:00 PHT.</p>
      <p>Each edition contains a limited set of story leads. There is no endless feed.</p>
      <ul class="install__list">
        <li>Previous / Next moves between stories.</li>
        <li>Full Story opens a QR code for the original article.</li>
        <li>After the final story, the edition page shows a QR code for the whole GOTO or TOGO companion page.</li>
        <li>The edition page is not counted as an additional story.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="install__note">
        Stories and reporting remain with GMA Network and GMA News Online. Each
        article link opens the original source.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>Updating</h2>
      <p>
        From v1.0.2 onward, new releases install over Wi-Fi: connect to Wi-Fi, then open
        Settings &rarr; System &rarr; Check for updates. The update keeps the same
        package you installed.
      </p>
      <p>You can also repeat the microSD steps above with a newer file.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <section class="install__section">
      <h2>Rollback</h2>
      <p>
        If you kept an official CrossPoint firmware image on your microSD card, you
        can use the same SD Card Firmware Update screen to select it.
      </p>
      <p>This is the intended rollback path.</p>
      <p>
        Use only official CrossPoint firmware intended for your exact XTEINK X4 model
        or revision.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />
    <p class="install__links">
      <a href={releaseUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download / GitHub release</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source code</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/goto/">Project GOTO</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .install {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
  }
  .install__back {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .install__head {
    border-bottom: var(--heavy-rule);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .install__head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }
  .install__lede {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.72;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  }
  .install__meta {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
  }
  .install__meta div {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35em var(--space-sm);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .install__meta dt {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    min-width: 6rem;
  }
  .install__meta dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  .install__sha {
    word-break: break-all;
  }
  .install__actions {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
  }
  .install__download {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.15rem;
    border: var(--heavy-rule);
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease;
  }
  .install__download:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }
  .install__section {
    margin-block: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .install__section h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .install__subhead {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-xs);
  }
  .install__section p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .install__caption-lead {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs) !important;
    color: var(--ink-faint) !important;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .install__list {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .install__list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .install__note {
    color: var(--ink-faint) !important;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .install__warn {
    color: var(--ink) !important;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .install__version code {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  .install__code {
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    overflow-x: auto;
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .install__code code {
    font-size: inherit;
    white-space: pre;
  }
  .install__figure {
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 0;
    max-width: 400px;
  }
  .install__figure--small {
    max-width: 260px;
  }
  .install__figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .install__figure figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .install__links {
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .install__links span {
    margin: 0 0.5em;
    color: var(--rule);
  }
</style>
